/*
 * data/ordinary.js -- the Mass Ordinary (Kyriale).
 *
 * GENERATED by sources/gregobase/build-ordinary.py -- re-run that rather than
 * hand-editing here.
 *
 * These chants are the one part of the repertoire that is NOT tied to a day: a
 * Kyriale Mass is chosen for a class of occasions, so app.js browses them by
 * Mass ("Browse: Mass Ordinary") rather than by date, the way it browses the
 * Common of Saints by category. The same Kyriale serves both calendars, so
 * unlike INTROITS/PROPERS there is no 1962 counterpart table and the
 * Modern/1962 toggle is hidden in this mode.
 *
 * Chants are the traditional Kyriale forms (Kyrie sung in threes, "iij."), not
 * GregoBase's shorter "forma ordinaria" rows.
 *
 * window.ORDINARY_MASSES  ordered picker list of { key, label, group }; `group`
 *                         becomes an <optgroup>, as in COMMON_CATEGORIES.
 * window.ORDINARY         { key: { part: entry } }, one level of nesting like
 *                         PROPERS. Entries carry the same fields as any other
 *                         proper (title/latin/translation/mode/reference/gabc/
 *                         source, optional blurb) plus an optional `tabLabel`
 *                         where the part's name isn't the chant's name -- Mass
 *                         XVII's dismissal is Benedicamus Domino, not Ite.
 *
 * The Latin is derived from each chant's own gabc lyrics by the build script,
 * so it cannot drift from the notation above it.
 */
